  "notes": "Piano-first topline-and-build pop architect, and a board entry rather than an artist one, so the drums and bass are authored hardest. The kit is the entry's: \"four-square kick with a big reverbed backbeat and layered claps; the signature is a percussion-only or clap-only pre-chorus that then detonates into the chorus. Fills are tom cascades and reversed cymbals rather than snare rolls.\" So the kick anchors all four beats, the snare sits under a large tail with a doubled clap stack, `rolls.freqPerBar` is 0 and the snare-roll ladder is off, the perc lanes are `tom`, `crash` and `reverse`, and the pre-chorus detonation is the deepest `dropOutBeats` this section authors. No `bass808` block: \"no 808 idiom. Sustained synth bass doubling the kick, with a sub swell as the chorus trigger\", which is `mirror_kick` at 0.96 with almost no passing motion. Harmony is his documented method — \"major-mode with a IV—V—vi—I lift cadence, and minor-mode i—VI—III—VII for the dance-facing work; he writes at the piano\" — so those two families lead over 4-bar diatonic loops. The melody block encodes the stated build: \"a narrow verse, a rhythmically accelerating pre-chorus and a wide-interval chorus that lands on a held note\", which is `long_arc` with a `densityPerBar` spread wide enough to accelerate, an arch contour and a raised `octaveJumpProb`; \"a stacked wordless vowel hook\" is the `sustain_pad` counter. ⚠ `confidence` is medium against a high-medium rating because the research says \"the tempo band is aggregated across credits\": every drum probability, the humanize numbers and `bpm.mode` 112 (the midpoint of the stated 100—125 anthem core) are INFERRED.",
